{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-5-5","id":"msg_011CgRyosRrrYtQpzfpZxQjv","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Your job has never reported anything because the script crashes before it sends any message. Under launchd it also can't log in to Claude, so there would be no review to send even without the crash. I fixed the script crash and made the notifier fail loudly. The login problem is still open and needs a check on your Mac.\n\n**What's wrong**\n\n1. **The script crashes on `status=$?`.** In zsh, `status` is a read-only special variable. Each run logs `read-only variable: status` to `nightly-review.err`, and the script exits before `notify.sh` runs. That's why you got no summary and no failure note.\n2. **`claude` says \"Not logged in\" on every run.** The plist sets only `PATH`, so anything your shell exports (such as an API key or config-dir variable) is missing under launchd. The snapshot doesn't show which it is, so I couldn't fix this part.\n3. **`notify.sh` can fail silently.** If the keychain lookup for the Telegram token fails, the script still exits 0 and sends nothing. This would hide the next problem.\n\n**What I changed** (in this directory only)\n\n- `bin/nightly-review.zsh`: renamed `status` to `rc`. The failure note now also points at `nightly-review.err`.\n- `bin/notify.sh`: the token lookup is an explicit assignment, and `curl -fsS` makes HTTP errors exit non-zero.\n\nI tested both scripts with stub `claude`, `security` and `curl` in a scratch HOME. Failure and success paths both send the right note, and a failed lookup stops the notifier. Nothing was sent to Telegram, and I didn't run the real job.\n\n**What you need to do**\n\n1. Copy the two scripts into `~/bin/`, keeping them executable.\n2. Check the login. In a clean environment, run `env -i HOME=\"$HOME\" PATH=/opt/homebrew/bin:/usr/local/bin:/usr/bin:/bin claude -p \"say ok\"`. If it says \"Not logged in\", run `/login` interactively and retry. Don't put API keys in the plist.\n3. Run `launchctl kickstart -k gui/$(id -u)/com.vk.nightly-review`. You should get a Telegram message, either a summary or a failure note with the reason.\n\nThe causes and these steps are in `ANSWER.md`. I haven't committed anything."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1870,"cache_read_input_tokens":33492,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1870},"output_tokens":5,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"6048fe72-277d-4c67-941f-de110b71e405","uuid":"a0fbefed-f346-485a-96a1-28efb86f5cca","timestamp":"2026-10-27T02:49:10.346Z","request_id":"req_011CgRyos4X5k3vZHcNuPqFw"}
